                                            "present"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f6a6f4e-7647-4b80-bd51-a3e737aed32d",
                                                "sense_id": "bd89aca7-8252-3963-b622-cd57babf9b9f",
                                                "text": "Since the mid-1980s, when Indonesia first began to clear its bountiful forests on an industrial scale in favour of lucrative palm-oil plantations, “haze” has become an almost annual occurrence in South-East Asia. The cheapest way to clear logged woodland is to burn it, producing an acrid cloud of foul white smoke that, carried by the wind, can cover hundreds, or even thousands, of square miles."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "df7c0b6b-7a37-425b-a271-59a98d0b37d4",
                        "source_entry_id": "fa2d4482-8061-33ad-94a8-2e975586e3d4",
                        "source_sense_id": "d977bcbb-65f9-315d-824f-9fd202b3638a",
                        "source_sense_description": "het maken, produceren van iets",
                        "target_lang_word": "manufacture",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "manufacture",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "186b14e5-c041-390c-a801-298a58ecd0d5",
                                        "entry_id": "1af70900-73b6-3945-972c-36a3c369a5f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The action or process of making goods systematically or on a large scale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3dbe4e1-3bc5-4953-9941-518e26947f3c",
                                                "sense_id": "186b14e5-c041-390c-a801-298a58ecd0d5",
                                                "text": "After years of exporting the gum base to be used as an ingredient in the manufacture of regular chewing gum, the cooperative recently decided to start making its own gum using only chicle gum base and natural flavorings and sweeteners"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7c19a5c-1040-3708-a248-9df1d568a2b1",
                                        "entry_id": "1af70900-73b6-3945-972c-36a3c369a5f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything made, formed or produced; product."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d0d96e4-9728-49e7-8c21-625dee9525b7",
                                                "sense_id": "a7c19a5c-1040-3708-a248-9df1d568a2b1",
                                                "text": "The roads [are] crowded with carriers, laden with rich manufactures."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63a8d25a-9932-41b4-afb3-b17f5cdae27d",
                                                "sense_id": "a7c19a5c-1040-3708-a248-9df1d568a2b1",
                                                "text": "Thus, a patented manufacture should be either better in quality or cheaper in cost than that which it is intended to supplant."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5db5dafe-a572-3ddc-85a7-028223140cc2",
                                        "entry_id": "1af70900-73b6-3945-972c-36a3c369a5f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The process of such production; generation, creation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9675ebf2-d6ec-4476-a809-c7c71cb31cec",
                                                "sense_id": "5db5dafe-a572-3ddc-85a7-028223140cc2",
                                                "text": "Our lawgivers take special pride in the ever active manufacture of new bills and laws."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b169e081-4dea-3858-8fd8-5701a9b9e81a",
                                        "entry_id": "1af70900-73b6-3945-972c-36a3c369a5f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A watch manufacturer that makes its own parts, rather than assembling watches from parts obtained from other firms."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "manufacture",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a77ec914-0047-3c4f-91b2-c10cdb171fd2",
                                        "entry_id": "eebe4468-642d-3e99-9bb8-2f2390da07ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make things, usually on a large scale, with tools and either physical labor or machinery."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73477c49-d9cc-452a-a675-34c17d945f42",
                                                "sense_id": "a77ec914-0047-3c4f-91b2-c10cdb171fd2",
                                                "text": "Scientists are learning how to manufacture sperm and egg cells from other types of cell; others are developing \"alternative\" wombs"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a10dd924-d5ef-3919-b36a-e828601e955f",
                                        "entry_id": "eebe4468-642d-3e99-9bb8-2f2390da07ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To work (raw or partly wrought materials) into suitable forms for use."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca723b3b-3365-4ddd-8cf3-7078227d96d1",
                                                "sense_id": "a10dd924-d5ef-3919-b36a-e828601e955f",
                                                "text": "to manufacture wool into blankets"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df16aa19-3efe-494f-9ae1-af800920e7fb",
                                                "sense_id": "a10dd924-d5ef-3919-b36a-e828601e955f",
                                                "text": "The instrument of this dumbing down in Nineteen Eighty-Four was Newspeak, the official language of the English Socialist Party (Ingsoc). Newspeak was a sort of Totalitarian Esperanto that sought gradually to diminish the range of what was thinkable by eliminating, contracting and manufacturing words."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21023bef-40d3-3c6f-9ba7-7002d2130007",
                                        "entry_id": "eebe4468-642d-3e99-9bb8-2f2390da07ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fabricate; to create false evidence to support a point."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9465031a-0998-46d1-9de0-dffdd623fa0c",
                                                "sense_id": "21023bef-40d3-3c6f-9ba7-7002d2130007",
                                                "text": "The collegian keeps manufacturing new excuses for their tardiness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a80b61e-d36a-47cd-a1b7-e22cfc5e91f6",
                                                "sense_id": "21023bef-40d3-3c6f-9ba7-7002d2130007",
                                                "text": "Digital technology has made it so easy to manufacture lies that it's become difficult to separate fact from fiction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
